From: turbo-boo <59400127+turbo-boo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 20:15:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Drop incompatible recorder cache for MOVIE

The recorder singleton is shared by ordinary Video and MOVIE.  VideoModule's
constructor reused it without checking the target mode, leaving MOVIE to reset
an ordinary recorder instead of constructing its Ib/t cinematic recorder.
The reset failure is delivered to RxJava without an error consumer, so camera
setup silently terminates with controls disabled.

Release the cached recorder during construction when the already-selected
module is MOVIE.  The normal cache path remains unchanged for all other video
modes.
---
 smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali b/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali
index 03225356..a686d3f4 100644
--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali
@@ -160,6 +160,18 @@
 
     move-result-object v1
 
+    invoke-static {}, Lcom/android/camera/module/P;->g()Z
+
+    move-result v2
+
+    if-eqz v2, :movie_cache_ready
+
+    const/4 v2, 0x0
+
+    invoke-virtual {v1, v2}, Lcom/android/camera/module/video/t;->b(I)V
+
+    :movie_cache_ready
+
     iget-object v2, v1, Lcom/android/camera/module/video/t;->b:Ljava/lang/Object;
 
     monitor-enter v2
-- 
